[[2047,31,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The main beam headlamps circuit is operated by the steering column\nswitch unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>When the switch is turned to the main beam\nposition, or when the &quot;flashing&quot; contact is closed, the\nline which supplies the (left) \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and (right) \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               headlamps\nreceives a supply controlled by the ignition. Each circuit is protected\nby a fuse for the junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F7</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              for the left\nlamp and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F6</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               for the right one.</p><p>The suppy line for the left headlamp also\nsends a signal to the rev counter module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (pin 4 of connector\nB) to light up the &quot;main beam headlamps on&quot; warning light.</p><p>The circuit for the main beam headlamps\nalso provides a signal (from pin 4, connector F of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) for\nkeeping the dipped headlamps on when the main beam headlamps are\non. (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3233782\">E2011</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              )</p>"]]